SI GAMES — changes.log
======================
Newest entry first. Markers: FIX = something broken, ADD = new thing,
CHG = behaviour changed, DEL = removed.

2026-11-13 — intent search, open comments, four new palettes
------------------------------------------------------------

ADD  AI search on the shelf: the query is read as intent instead of a
     substring. Concept groups (horror, racing, shooter, multiplayer...),
     synonyms, typo-tolerant title matching, "like Pac-Man" similarity search
     and a strip that shows how the sentence was understood, plus example
     prompts under an empty box. Runs on-device — no key, no network, no
     latency. src/lib/search.ts.

CHG  GTA V is fully in-frame now: every card goes through the webtoppings
     proxy. Server 1 — v2, Server 2 — v1 (its `{enter mode}` slot is filled by
     the Story / Sandbox / GTA VI / title cards), Server 3 — multiplayer v1 (no
     mode preset, so the game's title screen asks) and the new Server 4 —
     v1 pages (the pages.dev build). Version tags survive label redaction; host
     names still never reach the interface.

ADD  Grand Theft Auto IV (gta-iv), first on the new-games shelf: the ps2.playtab
     build at https://ps2.playtab.fun/gtfor/, using its playtab cover. It is
     tagged GTA / Open World / Driving and embedded in the frame.

CHG  Comments need no account at all now: a display name and an email are
     typed next to the comment. The email is stored for the one-per-person
     rule and never returned to any client. The (gameId, authorEmail) index is
     the actual guard; the browser also remembers its own comment locally.
     Ratings and likes still use the one-tap guest pass.

DEL  Extreme Driving Simulator — pulled from the library.

ADD  Four more palettes: Ember (magenta/ember), Aurora (emerald/ice), Royal
     (indigo/gold) and Steel (graphite/ice). Ten themes total; the picker
     scrolls when the menu is taller than the viewport.

ADD  The Uiverse rainbow ring spinner (mrhyddenn) on the boot screen and the
     route fallback, with position:relative added so the inner ring centres.

2026-11-12 — launch theatre, player signal, private sheet
---------------------------------------------------------

ADD  Launch theatre. Clicking Play hands the card's on-screen position to the
     player page (src/lib/launch.ts). The card flies into the console's
     cartridge slot, the CRT wakes around the real iframe (loading the whole
     time), the loaded game sits in the tube for 0.5s, then a FLIP zoom grows
     that same frame into the player layout — no reload, because the iframe is
     never moved, only transformed. Skipped for hand-over titles, external
     links and reduced-motion players (src/components/BootConsole.tsx).

ADD  Player signal under every game: 1-5 stars, a like, and one comment per
     player per game, with live counts on the library cards. Backed by Convex
     (`gameRatings` / `gameComments`) so the limit is enforced by the
     (gameId, userId) unique row, not just the UI. Guests can sign in with one
     anonymous tap; COMMENTS_PER_GAME_PER_PLAYER in src/lib/feedback.ts is the
     public limit constant.

ADD  Private data sheet at /sheet — unlisted, noindex, no nav link. Searchable
     table of every title with its cover/art URL, source link, mirrors, tags
     and type, plus CSV/JSON export and per-link copy/open buttons.

CHG  GTA V mirrors: the dead pages.dev build is gone and playgta5.com takes its
     place as Server 3. It answers with the browser build and is offered as a
     hand-over link (copy it, open your own tab) like Servers 1 and 2.

CHG  Crisper throughout: card hover lift and art zoom, staged grid entrance,
     focus-visible rings, sticky header shadow, floating hero console, a
     rebuilt boot screen (scanlines, horizon, INSERT/POWER/PLAY steps) and a
     route wipe between pages. Route motion is opacity-only so the boot
     console's fixed layers keep the viewport as their frame of reference.

2026-11-10 — library drop, cover art, change list and new-games pages
----------------------------------------------------------------------

ADD  94 new titles, all checked against the shelf first so no existing game
     gets a duplicate card. Headline pair: SMASHLINE and CHOMPOCALYPSE
     (RetroGems arcade racers, embedded in the frame). Behind them: StarCraft
     (OpenBW), Mario Kart 64 Online, Super Mario Galaxy, the Budokai line,
     Tekken 4/5, SSX 3, Soulcalibur II, Daggerfall, wipEout, PSO Reborn and
     the romhack compendiums. Data block: `featuredNewGames`, `importedGames`
     and `importedGameEntries` in src/data/games.ts.

ADD  Real cover art for the first 26 arrivals, from the confirmed page-one
     covers (COVERS map in games.ts). FIFA 14, NFS Underground 2, PES 2011 and
     Burnout 3 traded their old art for the confirmed files too.

CHG  Extra links for titles already on the shelf became server mirrors on the
     existing card instead of second cards (FIFA 14, Burnout 3, MK: Shaolin
     Monks, WWE HCTP, Tekken 5 DR, Guitar Hero 3, Halo CE, Mario Kart 64).
     Hosts that answer with X-Frame-Options / frame-ancestors carry
     `openInNewTab` and hand the link over; everything else runs in-frame.

ADD  Two paged shelves: /new lists the latest drop and /changelog lists these
     release notes. Both use the shared `Pager` component and keep the page
     number in the query string, so a page can be linked or reloaded. Linked
     from the header nav and from two shortcut cards under the library
     heading, since the header nav is hidden on phones.

FIX  HiddenSettings wrote state from an effect on every open, which the lint
     rule flags as a cascading render. The saved setting is now read in the
     open handler, so `bun run lint` is back to 0 errors.

2026-10-26 — code health, colour themes, six new titles
-------------------------------------------------------

ADD  Colour themes (6 palettes, header switcher)
     The whole shell now paints from CSS custom properties instead of
     hardcoded hex: --si-accent*, --si-glow*, --si-bg, --si-panel* etc.
     A theme is only a re-declaration of those tokens on
     :root[data-theme="…"], so one rule set recolours cards, buttons,
     borders, the player, the boot screen and the launch pages.
       · Nebula  — neon blue / violet (the original palette, unchanged)
       · Plasma  — violet / hot pink
       · Crimson — red / amber
       · Tidal   — azure / aqua
       · Toxic   — green / lime
       · Solar   — orange / gold
     Switcher: src/components/ThemePicker.tsx (header, next to the status
     line). Logic: src/lib/themes.ts. Selection persists in localStorage
     under "si-games-theme" and is applied before first paint from
     main.tsx, so there is no flash of the wrong palette. The browser
     chrome (theme-color meta) follows the active theme, and the landing
     starfield re-tints itself too (--si-star-hot / --si-star-cool, plus a
     "si-theme-change" window event from applyTheme()).

ADD  Six new titles to the library (all verified reachable and served
     without X-Frame-Options / frame-ancestors, so they load in-frame):
       · Slither.io      — slither.io        (Arcade, .io)
       · Shell Shockers  — shellshock.io     (Shooter, FPS)
       · Surviv.io       — surviv.io         (Shooter, Battle Royale)
       · Sandspiel       — sandspiel.club    (Sandbox, falling sand)
       · Hextris         — hextris.github.io (Puzzle, stacking)
       · Skribbl.io      — skribbl.io        (Party, drawing)
     Each carries a description, a real control map and a generated star
     cover (no new remote image dependencies).

FIX  Header layout — the stylesheet has always targeted a
     `.site-header .header-inner` wrapper (the mobile breakpoint sets its
     width) but no such element existed, so brand, nav and status rendered
     as full-width blocks stacked flush against the viewport edge. The
     wrapper is back in Landing.tsx, laid out as a centred flex row on
     desktop (min(1120px, 100% - 40px), matching the main column) and
     keeping the existing mobile width rule working.

FIX  Lint went from 12 errors to 0 (`bun run lint` now exits clean; the
     remaining 21 warnings are the pre-existing react-refresh notices on
     template/vendor files):
       · Dashboard.tsx      — dropped unused CardDescription + Navigate
                              imports.
       · games.ts           — applyLibraryPatch destructured a `lead`
                              marker it never used (x2); replaced with an
                              explicit id/label/url/external projection.
       · Landing.tsx        — favorites/recent were read from localStorage
                              in a mount effect (setState-in-effect); they
                              are now lazy useState initialisers. The
                              "reset pagination when filters change"
                              effect became applyQuery / applyCategory /
                              applySortBy callbacks, so paging resets
                              exactly where the filter changes.
       · GamePlayer.tsx     — the [game] effect synchronised six pieces of
                              state on every title change. The player is
                              now keyed by resolvedId, so switching games
                              remounts it: all of that state is initial
                              state again, and the effect only records the
                              visit in "si-games-recent". Favorites also
                              moved to a lazy initialiser.
       · InstallerAd.tsx    — dismissal flag read from localStorage in an
                              effect → lazy initialiser; useEffect import
                              removed.
       · use-mobile.ts      — window.matchMedia + setState-in-effect →
                              useSyncExternalStore (subscribes properly,
                              no state sync in the body).
       · ui/carousel.tsx    — setApi and the first scroll-flag read were
                              synchronous setState in effect bodies; both
                              now hand over after the effect settles. The
                              "reInit" listener was registered but never
                              removed — cleanup now offs it too.
       · ui/sidebar.tsx     — SidebarMenuSkeleton called Math.random()
                              inside a useMemo during render; the width is
                              now picked once per instance in a lazy
                              useState initialiser.

CHG  src/index.css and src/player-prompt.css: every accent, glow, panel and
     surface hex (5608f8, 3efeff, 4320e0, 0d1527, 060e22, 131e36, 182645,
     1a2b55, 0a142e, 101a35, 1e2d55, 7ff9ff …) now resolves through a
     token, including the translucent variants (--si-accent-18 … -88,
     --si-glow-12 … -40). Neutral values (text greys, the yellow SI
     Installer block, dark overlays) were deliberately left alone.


